1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:01,600
The name is the method.

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:03,860
The failure mode.

3
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:07,280
You backtest a strategy and it loses.

4
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:10,520
Change the window, add a filter, run it

5
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:10,820
again,

6
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:12,250
change something else.

7
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:15,810
Each variation is defensible on its own, but

8
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:18,900
nobody keeps a ledger of every variation.

9
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:20,780
No one can say which one produced the

10
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:21,200
numbers.

11
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:24,660
Three identical runs, one survivor,

12
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,780
no label for which is real.

13
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:31,840
The fix comes from clinical trials, preregistration.

14
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:35,480
Before the run, you write down three things,

15
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:39,040
the hypothesis in one falsifiable sentence,

16
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:40,220
the data,

17
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:41,640
and the bar,

18
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:43,890
a number to clear after costs.

19
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:46,120
The document goes to Git.

20
00:00:46,550 --> 00:00:48,120
The commit is the seal,

21
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:50,200
and Git is the notary.

22
00:00:51,160 --> 00:00:54,120
After that, the document is append only.

23
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:56,280
Anyone can diff it against the run config

24
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,420
to check nothing moved.

25
00:00:58,330 --> 00:01:00,340
The commitment is the point.

26
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:02,410
Four states,

27
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:07,040
the prereg, hypothesis, data, and bar written down

28
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:08,140
before anything runs.

29
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:09,460
The seal,

30
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:11,660
the commit that locks the document.

31
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:13,260
The verdict,

32
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:16,700
the result judged by the preregistered criteria,

33
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:18,180
not by how it looks.

34
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:21,820
Confirmed, falsified, or inconclusive.

35
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:23,500
Then the scoreboard,

36
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:25,980
every prereg in one public table

37
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:27,980
and an arrow back to the prereg.

38
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:30,460
The postmortem becomes the next prereg.

39
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:33,610
Every video on this channel lives inside this

40
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:34,140
diagram.

41
00:01:35,290 --> 00:01:37,390
What does sealed mean in practice?

42
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:41,400
After the commit, the document is append only,

43
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,080
and the Git history is the audit trail.

44
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:46,180
The same rule holds for runs.

45
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:48,140
A result counts only if it matches the

46
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:48,900
sealed config.

47
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:52,260
The seal is one command on screen now.

48
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:55,720
The commit produces a SHA recorded in the

49
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:57,200
document and on the scoreboard.

50
00:01:57,750 --> 00:01:59,870
The SHA on screen is the commit that

51
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:01,160
first committed this spec,

52
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:04,560
the channel's first sealed artifact.

53
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:06,960
If the scoreboard shows a different one, that

54
00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:07,460
is a bug.

55
00:02:08,589 --> 00:02:09,280
The bar,

56
00:02:10,060 --> 00:02:12,040
a number to reach after costs.

57
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:15,370
The chart draws the cost-adjusted series,

58
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:17,730
then the bar, an amber line

59
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:18,559
last.

60
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:21,640
The value in the tag is an example

61
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:23,100
labeled on screen.

62
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:25,900
No results document exists yet.

63
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,360
The bar is drawn the same way whether

64
00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:31,240
the strategy passes or fails.

65
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:33,440
Same chart, same bar.

66
00:02:34,309 --> 00:02:37,440
The only difference is where the curve ends

67
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:38,500
relative to the line,

68
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,980
and that is the story.

69
00:02:42,110 --> 00:02:44,040
The scoreboard is the product.

70
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:46,060
One table,

71
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:48,140
each row a prereg

72
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:51,480
with its ID, hypothesis, seal date,

73
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:52,450
verdict,

74
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:56,620
out-of-sample number, and link to results.

75
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:59,230
The rows on screen are examples labeled as

76
00:02:59,040 --> 00:02:59,540
such.

77
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,700
Above the table, the aggregate rows.

78
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:07,600
Total preregs, the confirmed, falsified, and inconclusive counts,

79
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:10,500
and the confirmation rate against a null baseline,

80
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:14,020
the fraction random strategies pass by chance.

81
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,760
Below the table, the composite,

82
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,700
the strategies the owner decides to trade.

83
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:22,920
Until the first pin, it is dormant,

84
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:24,400
and the label says so.

85
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:28,020
The same four lines on every video.

86
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:31,640
Educational content, not investment advice.

87
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:35,460
Backtest results are estimates under stated assumptions.

88
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:38,260
Live performance will differ, possibly badly.

89
00:03:39,070 --> 00:03:41,430
Preregistration controls data snooping.

90
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:44,640
It does not control overfitting in pre-seal choices,

91
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:47,140
data quality, or market regime change.

92
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:52,270
Past performance, including preregistered, costed, out-of-sample past performance,

93
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:54,540
is the weakest predictor in finance.

94
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:57,780
Same inputs, same pixels.

95
00:03:58,550 --> 00:04:00,800
The video pipeline is held to the same

96
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:02,710
reproducibility bar as the research.

97
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,490
If you cannot reproduce a number from this

98
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,060
repository, it is a bug
